Fub patch 0008-nessuna-radice-e-tabelle (UPSTREAM-API, to be proposed upstream).

An engine that does not touch the disk, and its global tables counted and
released (Fub plan K6, T28; docs/architecture/disegno-completo.md#il-disco).

- engine/src/file_access.rs: AutomationRoots::deny_all(), empty roots that
  are in force: check_read and check_write refuse every path with their error
  (at cfb30d81 AutomationRoots::new(&[], &[]) returns None, and without roots
  nothing is checked). With roots in force, the placed-document MEMO
  (doc/src/placed_document.rs) does not read the disk.
- text/src/fontdb/dirs.rs: set_system_fonts(false) empties the system font
  folders: no scan and no fallback reads the disk.
- engine/src/tables.rs (new): the global tables that grow with use, each with
  its weight (<table>_bytes) and its release (release_<table>), in order:

  crate                 table            Fub map family   releasable
  vectorcraft-render    image_cache      immagini         yes
  vectorcraft-render    placed_bitmaps   formati          yes
  vectorcraft-render    halftone_cache   immagini         yes
  vectorcraft-doc       placed_files     formati          yes
  vectorcraft-doc       placed_reads     formati          yes
  vectorcraft-effects   texture_cache    raster           yes
  vectorcraft-color     user_profiles    colore           no
  vectorcraft-text      font_faces       testo            no

  user_profiles and font_faces cannot be released without breaking the open
  documents that use them: their weight still counts (Fub DECISIONS.md, T28).
  Left out, and the module says why: fixed-size tables (catalogs), glyph and
  outline caches with their own cap, settings, per-thread caches, the MEMO
  under deny_all, the recovery blob names and the plug-in intern.

